<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tauekel Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1598</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Tawakkul Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tauekel Khan was khan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakhs</a> in the late sixteenth century, ruling until 1598. A son of Shigai Khan, he took advantage of the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-khan-ii">Abdullah Khan II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> to seize <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkistan-city">Turkistan</a> and other towns of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syr-darya">Syr Darya</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaybanids">Shaybanids</a> in 1598. He died of wounds received in a campaign against Bukhara the same year, and his gains were largely kept by his brother and successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esim-khan">Esim Khan</a>.</p></div>
